Player movement (all numbers go in constants.ts)
Body. Standing hitbox 20×30 px. Flat hitbox 28×10 px. Gravity 1800 px/s², max fall speed 900 px/s.
Run. Idle-to-run only, no walk. Max speed 260 px/s, ground acceleration 2200, ground deceleration 2600, air acceleration 1600, air deceleration 1200. Turning around on the ground plays a short skid with 3 paper-triangle particles.
Jump. Jump velocity −560 px/s (about 87 px, 2.7 tiles, at full hold). Releasing the button early multiplies upward speed by 0.45 so a tap gives about 1.2 tiles. Falling uses gravity ×1.6. At the apex (|vy| < 60) gravity is ×0.5 for a floaty hang. Coyote time 90 ms and jump buffer 110 ms. Player cannot step up onto anything taller than 87 px by jumping, and the level relies on that.
Dash. Horizontal only, in the facing direction (or held direction). Speed 560 px/s for 150 ms (≈84 px), gravity off during the dash, then keep 40% of the speed for 80 ms. One air dash, refreshed on landing; ground dash allowed; cooldown 350 ms. Freeze the game 40 ms at dash start for punch.
Flat form (hold S). Hitbox shrinks to 28×10 over 0.12 s. Entering while running keeps momentum: start at up to 320 px/s and decay with friction 700 to a flat max speed of 200 px/s (a slide). Cannot jump, dash or use the sword while flat. On releasing S the player stays flat until there is at least 30 px of headroom, then unfolds automatically (test a 20×30 rect against solids). Flat form must never trap the player: if both folding and unfolding are blocked, Backspace resets.
State machine. idle, run, skid, jumpUp, apex, fall, land, dash, flat. Each state has an enter and exit function. Show the current state in the debug overlay.
Game feel
Character art. The player is built from separate triangles like a low-poly paper figure: a large triangle head, a triangle neck/chest, a triangle torso, triangle arms and two-piece triangle legs. Fill #7FC49A, outline #1E8A4C, outline width 2 px. Pieces are drawn in code and rotate independently.
Animation (procedural, no sprites).
• Idle: slow breathing (torso scale 1.0→1.03 at 0.5 Hz), head bob, and every few seconds a small arm shrug.
• Run: leg triangles swing, torso leans 8° into the run, arms counter-swing.
• Jump up: stretch to 1.15 tall. Fall: stretch to 1.1 tall, legs trail upward.
• Land: squash to 1.2 wide × 0.8 tall for 90 ms, spring back, 4–6 triangle dust pieces.
• Dash: stretch to 1.4 wide, spawn a triangle afterimage every 25 ms that fades over 180 ms.
• Flat: the figure folds down to a thin diamond sliver with a short fold animation.
• Reset or death: the figure bursts into its triangles, they spin outward then re-fold at the checkpoint in 0.5 s.
Camera. Follows the player with smoothing (lerp 0.12), look-ahead of 80 px in the facing 1.0→1.03 for 120 ms on pickup.direction (lerped), vertical deadzone 60 px, clamped to level bounds. Slight zoom pulse 
Screen shake. 2 px for 80 ms when landing from more than 4 tiles, 3 px for 100 ms when a fold platform slams open.
Particles. Every effect uses small triangles (paper shards), not circles: footsteps, landing, dash trail, fold dust, wind streaks, pickup sparkle.
Audio (Web Audio, started on first key press, M to mute). Footstep: 20 ms filtered noise tick every 0.28 s while running. Jump: rising noise whoosh. Land: low noise thud. Dash: band-pass noise sweep 800→3000 Hz over 120 ms. Fold or unfold: short crinkle (gated noise bursts). Switch: click plus a soft 660 Hz sine chime. Fan: looping low filtered noise whose volume follows distance. Pickup: triangle-wave arpeggio 523, 659, 784 Hz. Keep everything quiet and soft.
Visual style
Calm and clean, like paper on paper. Background mint #C9E4D1 with a very faint grid of fold lines. Solid platforms cream #F7F2E8 with dark ink outline #2B2A33, 2 px, with one lighter triangle facet drawn across the top of each platform for a low-poly feel. Ground below the floor is filled paper cream with diagonal fold lines.
Colour language (keep it consistent): purple #8B7FD6 = fold pieces and switches, amber #F0A93B = wind, teal #2FA58A = form pieces (slits and pickups). Interactive objects pulse softly (0.8 Hz glow) until used.
HUD and screens
• Title screen: "Unfolded", a Play button, and a Room select list: Movement lane, 1A Fold, 1B Flat, 1C Wind. Selecting a room starts it directly.
• In-game HUD: small room name top-left (for example "1A · Fold"), reset counter and room timer top-right. Nothing else.
• Paper "tag" prompts placed in the world, with drawn key caps, fading in near the spot where they matter and out afterward.
• End screen after Level 1: "Level complete", time, resets, and a "Play again" button.
Level 1 layout
World is 92 tiles wide, 18 tall (2944×576 px). The main floor surface is at row 14 (y = 448 px). Below, h means tiles above the main floor, negative is below it. Checkpoints sit at the start of each section.
Movement lane (x 0–24), teaches run, jump, dash
• Floor h=0 from x 0 to 24. Player spawns at x 3. Prompt at x 3: "A / D run".
• Low step at x 8–9, h 0–1 (1 tile). Prompt: "Space: jump".
• Taller block at x 13–14, h 0–2. Prompt: "Hold Space for higher".
• Dash gap: the floor stops at x 18 and resumes at x 24, so the gap is 6 tiles (192 px). The pit floor is at h −2, safe, and the player can always jump out of either side (wall is 64 px, jump is 87 px). Prompt at the edge: "Shift in the air: dash". With these numbers a full jump covers about 4.5 tiles and jump plus dash about 7.2 tiles, so the gap needs a dash but has at least a tile of margin. If it fails that check in play, adjust the gap and tell me.
Room 1A: Fold (x 24–46)
• Floor h=0 from x 24 to 46. Checkpoint at x 25.
• Switch (pressure plate, latches when pressed) at x 27, floor level, purple, pulsing. Prompt: "Step on it".
• Folded stairs (three FoldPlatforms, each 2 tiles wide), drawn folded as dashed purple outlines with no collision: step 1 at x 31–32, top h=1; step 2 at x 34–35, top h=2; then a solid ledge block from x 37 to 46 with its top at h=3 (96 px). Without the stairs the ledge is unreachable (jump is 87 px).
• When the switch is pressed: a purple ripple spreads from the plate and a dotted purple line draws from the switch to each step; the steps unfold one after another (0.12 s apart), each rotating around its crease with angle-based shading, landing with a small dust burst and shake, and collision turns on when each lands.
• The ledge's right edge drops 3 tiles (96 px) onto the next room's floor, which is safe.
Room 1B: Flat form (x 46–68)
• Floor h=0 from x 46 to 68. Checkpoint at x 47.
• A tall pillar from x 54 to 60, from h=0.44 (14 px above the floor) up to h=7, solid. The 14 px gap under it is the slit, 6 tiles (192 px) long. The slit has a teal glowing outline and a small chevron marker. Prompt at x 51: "Hold S: fold flat".
• The player cannot go over the pillar (7 tiles) and cannot pass standing, only flat. Passing through takes about 1 s at flat speed.
• Optional reinforcement: a second, shorter slit pillar at x 63–65 with the same 14 px clearance.
Room 1C: Wind (x 68–92)
• Floor h=0 from x 68 to 72. Checkpoint at x 69.
• Pit from x 72 to 82, floor at h −2 (safe; the player can jump out on the left side).
• Fan on the pit floor at x 77–78 (2 tiles wide). Its draught column is x 77–78, from the pit floor up to 8 tiles (256 px). Inside the column the player's vertical speed accelerates toward −320 px/s with acceleration 2400 and gravity is ignored; horizontal control stays active (so the player can steer). At the top of the column the player floats a little and can drift right.
• High platform from x 82 to 92 with its top at h=4 (128 px), solid. It cannot be reached from the floor or the pit floor by jumping, only by riding the draught.
• Sword pieces: three small floating teal triangles orbiting the point x 88, h 5.5.
• Exit door at x 91, a folded paper door that unfolds when the player gets near.
• Visuals: blades of the fan are rotating triangles; the column is filled with amber triangles rising at about 14 per second; when the player is inside, streaks swirl around them.
Level end
Touching the sword pieces: they swirl, then orbit the player (pulse, zoom 1.03, pickup arpeggio). A prompt appears: "Press R". Pressing R makes the pieces fold into a sword (a long thin triangle blade) with a bright whoosh; pressing R again turns it back into orbiting pieces. Left click or J plays a slash animation in the air with a small shake, but there is nothing to hit yet. Walking to the exit door finishes the level.
Level data
Define the level as plain data so rooms can be edited without touching the logic. Every entity has type, x, y (in tiles) and the room links by id:
export const level1 = {
  width: 92, height: 18, floorRow: 14,
  spawn: { x: 3, h: 0 },
  solids: [ { x: 0, w: 18, h: 0 }, { x: 24, w: 22, h: 0 } /* ... */ ],
  entities: [
    { id: 'sw1', type: 'Switch', x: 27, h: 0, targets: ['s1', 's2'] },
    { id: 's1', type: 'FoldPlatform', x: 31, w: 2, topH: 1, startsFolded: true },
    { id: 's2', type: 'FoldPlatform', x: 34, w: 2, topH: 2, startsFolded: true },
    { id: 'f1', type: 'Fan', x: 77, w: 2, floorH: -2, columnH: 8 },
    { id: 'slit1', type: 'Slit', x: 54, w: 6, clearancePx: 14 },
    { id: 'cp1', type: 'Checkpoint', x: 25, h: 0 }
  ]
};
Write the rest of the data (solids, pickups, exit, prompts) in the same style.
Reset and anti-softlock rules
• Backspace or the pause menu "Restart room" resets the current room instantly: player to the room's checkpoint, fold states and switches restored, no loading.
• No death and no hazards in Level 1. Pits are shallow and climbable.
• The player can never end up in an unrecoverable state; if they think they have, Backspace fixes it.
Debug overlay (F1)
Show FPS, player state, velocity, coyote and buffer timers, hitbox outlines, and whether the dash is available. Also add a small live tuning panel that edits the values in constants.ts at runtime (run speed, gravity, jump velocity, dash distance, coyote and buffer times), so I can change feel while playing.
Acceptance checklist
• Movement feels tight and responsive; coyote time and jump buffering work; a tap gives a short hop and a hold a full jump.
• The dash gap in the movement lane cannot be crossed without the dash and can be crossed with a normal jump plus dash.
• Room 1A cannot be finished without pressing the switch; the steps unfold in sequence with visible feedback.
• Room 1B can only be passed by folding flat; unfolding happens automatically with headroom.
• Room 1C can only be finished by riding the draught; falling in the pit never traps the player.
• Sword pieces turn into a sword on R and back on R.
• Backspace resets any room instantly. Room select works from the title screen.
• No console errors, no external assets.